.Dd September 16, 2026
.Dt NDI_PROP_REMOVE 9F
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ndi_prop_remove ,
.Nm ndi_prop_remove_all
.Nd remove hardware properties
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/sunndi.h
.Ft "int"
.Fo ndi_prop_remove
.Fa "dev_t dev"
.Fa "dev_info_t *dip"
.Fa "char *name"
.Fc
.Ft "void"
.Fo ndi_prop_remove_all
.Fa "dev_info_t *dip"
.Fc
.Sh INTERFACE LEVEL
illumos specific
.Pq Consolidation Private .
.Sh PARAMETERS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Va dev
Device number used when creating the property, or \fBDDI_DEV_T_NONE\fP
for a node property.
\fBDDI_DEV_T_ANY\fP is not permitted.
.It Va dip
Device node whose hardware properties are removed.
.It Va name
Nonempty, null-terminated property name.
.El
.Sh DESCRIPTION
\fBndi_prop_remove()\fP removes the hardware property identified by the exact
device number \fBdev\fP and property name \fBname\fP from \fBdip\fP.
It does not search ancestors.
.Pp
\fBndi_prop_remove_all()\fP removes all hardware properties from \fBdip\fP and clears
its dynamic parent-property description.
Driver and system properties are separate lists and are not removed.
The caller must keep \fBdip\fP valid throughout the operation.
.Sh CONTEXT
These functions may be called from user, kernel, or low-level interrupt
context.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
\fBndi_prop_remove()\fP returns \fBDDI_PROP_SUCCESS\fP, \fBDDI_PROP_NOT_FOUND\fP,
or \fBDDI_PROP_INVAL_ARG\fP.
\fBndi_prop_remove_all()\fP has no return value.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ndi_prop_update 9F ,
.Xr sunndi 9F
